# Walk-forward CV only

Time-series labels are autocorrelated. Random splits leak future into past.

## Rules

1. Use one of `WalkForwardSplit`, `PurgedKFold`, or `CombinatorialPurgedKFold`
   from `app/core/ai/training/splitters.py`. No `sklearn.model_selection.KFold`
   on time-series data.
2. `PurgedKFold` and `CombinatorialPurgedKFold` need the `t1` series (label
   realisation timestamps from `triple_barrier`). Pass it.
3. Embargo (`embargo_pct`) is mandatory — default 0.01. Setting it to 0
   defeats the purpose.
4. Walk-forward refits are mandatory for any model that goes to paper or live.
   No "trained once on 2010-2020, run on 2024" deployments.
5. When sweeping hyperparameters, multiple-testing inflation is real. Apply
   `deflated_sharpe(...)` from `app/core/ai/training/metrics.py` and report
   the deflated number.

## Smells to reject

- `train_test_split(X, y)` on bars
- A CV that returns higher-Sharpe folds without an embargo
- Backtests that report only the un-deflated Sharpe of the best sweep
